title: "Headroom: consumer GPU frequency-efficiency sweeps with voltage telemetry"
type: dataset
version: 1.2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23547564
date-released: 2026-10-21
authors:
  - family-names: "Chuang"
    given-names: "Zi Chen Raymond"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - GPU
  - DVFS
  - energy efficiency
  - frequency scaling
  - voltage-frequency curve
  - NVIDIA GeForce
  - measurement dataset
abstract: >-
  1088 locked-clock frequency sweeps on four consumer NVIDIA GPUs (RTX 5060 Ti, RTX 3070 Ti,
  RTX 2060 Super, RTX 3060) across three architectures, with throughput, board power and clocks
  per target frequency, and HWiNFO core-voltage and crossbar-clock extracts for 729 sweeps.
  Version 1.2.0 adds, counted separately, a registered five-day repeatability study (40 sweeps) and
  four pilot sessions of a registered energy-counter polling study (sizing data, no verdict), both on
  the RTX 5060 Ti. One physical card per model.
